# Server hexagonal architecture (ports & adapters)

Dependencies point **inward**. Inner layers never name outer types (Express, Kysely, pg-boss, SDKs). See README Architecture for infra details.

## Layer map

| Concept | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Domain | `core/` — entities, domain services, errors, constants, values |
| Use cases | `app/command`, `app/query`, `app/saga` |
| Driven ports | `app/port` — `*Repository`, `AppLogger`, `Lock` |
| Driving adapters | `web/` (HTTP/WS); job workers that invoke commands |
| Driven adapters | `adapter/` — Postgres repos, job queue, logger, lock |
| Composition root | `index.ts` + `adapter/factory.ts` |
| Shared | `shared/` — inward-only helpers |

Handlers call exported commands/queries (no separate inbound-port interfaces).

## Hard rules

- **`core/` / `shared/`**: no `#web`, `#adapter`, `#app`, Express, Kysely, pg-boss, or I/O.
- **`app/`**: no `#web`, SQL/Kysely, or concrete `Postgres*`; depend on port types + domain; thin orchestration only.
- **`web/`**: validate → command/query → map `@eoneom/api-client`; no repos, domain policy, or SQL.
- **`adapter/`**: implement ports; map to/from entities; no domain business rules.
- New outbound need → port in `app/port` → `adapter` impl → wire in Factory / `index.ts`.
- Ports use domain language (`BuildingUpgradeQueueRepository`), not tech (`SqlQuery`).

## Core: entities vs domain services

Do not conflate domain service, application use case, and adapter.

**Entity** (`*Entity` extends `BaseEntity`): identity + state + invariants for that concept. Prefer methods on the entity when the rule is about *this* object's state. Style: private constructor, `static create()`, `readonly` fields, methods return new instances. No I/O / Factory / ports. Avoid anemic bags—don't push single-entity invariants into commands or domain services.

**Domain service** (`core/*/service.ts`): use when logic does not belong on one entity, spans multiple concepts/constants, or is stateless pure calculation (`PricingService`, `BuildingService.getEarningsBySecond`). Pure + stateless (static methods); no DB/ports/Factory. Don't dump all logic here. Commands call domain code; don't re-implement pricing/requirements/upgrade rules inline.

```
One entity's own state/invariants? → Entity method
Pure/stateless spanning concepts/constants? → Domain service
Orchestration (load, persist, jobs, events, tx)? → app/ command/query/saga
Else → value / constant / error
```

## Where new work goes

- Domain → `core/<context>/` (`entity`, `service`, `error`, `constant`, `value`)
- Writes → `app/command/...` + `runCommand`
- Reads → `*Query` extending `GenericQuery`
- HTTP → `web/handler/...` + `router.ts`
- Persistence → port + `Postgres*` + Factory wiring
- Names: `*Entity`, `*Service`, `*Repository` / `Postgres*Repository`, kebab commands, `*Handler`, `*Query`, logs like `'building:cancel-queued-upgrade'`

## Factory (accepted shortcut)

Use `Factory.getRepository()` / `getLogger()` / etc. in commands (returns port types). Do **not** import concrete adapters (`Postgres*`, Kysely, Express) from `app/` or `core/`. Prefer new ports + Factory wiring over new `#adapter/...` implementation imports. Wire only in `index.ts` / Factory—not in handlers.

## Examples

```typescript
// BAD — core → adapter
import { PostgresBuildingRepository } from '#adapter/database/repository/building'

// BAD — handler owns persistence
await db.insertInto('building').values(...).execute()

// BAD — anemic: command owns entity invariant
if (building.level >= MAX) throw ...
building.level += 1

// BAD — domain service does I/O
static async upgrade(repo: Repository) { await repo.building.update(...) }

// GOOD — driving adapter → use case
await cancelQueuedBuildingUpgrade({ city_id, queue_id })

// GOOD — use case via Factory (port type)
const repository = Factory.getRepository()

// GOOD — entity owns transition
building.assertCanUpgrade({ is_building_in_progress })
const next = building.finishUpgrade()

// GOOD — pure domain service; command orchestrates
PricingService.getBuildingCost({ code, level, ... })
```
